<title>UK: Spain ups 6.0 pct Jan 2008 bond to 1.50 bln euros.</title>
<headline>Spain ups 6.0 pct Jan 2008 bond to 1.50 bln euros.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain has increased to 1.5 billion euros from 1.25 billion euros the size of its 6.00 percent January 2008 bond launched earlier, joint lead managers Banco Central Hispano, Paribas, Santander de Negocios and SBC Warburg said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal was due to be priced later at a spreadof 15 basis points over French Ecu OATs.</p>
<p> + + +</p>
<p> AMT   1.50 BLN EURO  COUPON     6.00	MATURITY    31.JAN.08</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    31.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+15 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1	   SALE LIMITS US/GB</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    SPANISH   HOME CTRY  SPAIN     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND APR.07 ECU OAT / APR.22 ECU OAT</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER</p>
<p>		OBLIGATIONS PAID/RECEIVED IN ECU UNTIL EMU WHEN IT</p>
<p>		WILL BE EXCHANGEABLE INTO OUTSTANDING BONO ISSUE.</p>
<p>		SHORT FIRST COUPON.</p>
